21. Towards sustainable financing of projects for decarbonization and adaptation of the economy to climate change:
a) by December 1, 2025, develop a National Program for the Formation of a "Green Financing" System in the Republic of Uzbekistan;
b) take measures to attract, starting in 2025, concessional loans and grants to support green and low-carbon development projects from the following sources:
from the European Bank for Reconstruction and Development - up to €200 million in stages;
from the World Bank - US$10 million to reduce methane emissions in the energy sector;
as part of technical assistance from the Korea International Cooperation Agency through the Global Green Development Institute - US$6.5 million to strengthen green cooperation between Uzbekistan and Korea;
as part of the World Bank's iCRAFT project - US$7.5 million through the sale of 500,000 tons of reduced greenhouse gases;
From the German Society for International Cooperation - 20 million euros for greening industry and reducing harmful gases emitted into the atmosphere by nitric acid production plants;
